  "security_implications": "The chunk computes decoy_data from entropy_i[1] via permutation and replication, used for side‑channel protection of KMAC operations. It also derives round select signals adv_sel, id_sel, gen_sel by subtracting cnt from last‑round constants. If cnt exceeds those constants (unsigned underflow), the selection signals become unexpectedly large values, potentially pointing to incorrect round buffers or invalid states. This could leak secret material or disrupt key‑derivation integrity. Additionally, if entropy_i[1] is predictable, the decoy mask becomes ineffective, weakening side‑channel resistance.",
